.TH DOCKER-HELPER-CONFIG 5
.SH NAME
docker-helper-config \- docker-helper configuration file format
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /etc/docker-helper/config.json
.br
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docker-helper/config.json
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B docker-helper
uses a JSON configuration file to control daemon behavior. The file location
depends on deployment mode:
.IP \(bu 4
\fISystem mode\fR: \fI/etc/docker-helper/config.json\fR
.IP \(bu 4
\fIUser mode\fR: \fI$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docker-helper/config.json\fR (defaults to ~/.config/docker-helper/config.json)
.PP
The environment variable \fBDOCKER_HELPER_CONFIG\fR can override the config path.
.SH CONFIGURATION FILES
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/config.json
System mode configuration (root-owned)
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/admin.token
System mode admin token (root-owned, mode 0600)
.TP
.B /var/lib/docker-helper/docker-helper.db
System mode state database
.TP
.B /run/docker-helper/docker-helper.sock
System mode Unix socket (created at runtime)
.SH FORMAT
JSON object with the following fields. Two fields are required; all others are optional.
.SH FIELDS
.TP
.B allowed_root (string, required)
Absolute path for agent workspace root. A new workspace root must satisfy
the following policy:
.RS 4
\(bu
be a non-empty absolute path;
\(bu
exist and be a directory;
\(bu
not be /;
\(bu
not be or descend into a system namespace.
.RE
.PP
Forbidden namespaces (the root itself and all descendants):
.br
/bin /boot /dev /etc /lib /lib32 /lib64 /libx32 /proc /root /run /sbin /sys /usr /var /tmp
.PP
The following namespaces are forbidden at the root but permit descendants:
.br
/home (e.g., /home/alice/work is allowed)
.br
/srv /opt /mnt /media (e.g., /srv/workspaces is allowed)
.PP
A symlink whose canonical target enters a forbidden namespace is rejected.
.PP
New workspace roots are resolved to their canonical path through symlink
resolution before policy evaluation; the canonical path is the effective
and stored root.
.PP
Existing stale AppArmor roots remain removable even if they no longer
satisfy the current policy.
.PP
In system mode, the initial value is added to managed AppArmor roots during
\fBdocker-helper init\fR. Subsequent changes require manual AppArmor updates
via \fBdocker-helper apparmor root\fR.
.TP
.B session_ttl (string, required)
Session time-to-live using Go duration syntax (e.g., "30m", "1h", "12h").
Must be a positive duration. An absent or empty field is invalid.
\fBdocker-helper init\fR creates this field with the value "12h".
.TP
.B log_level (string, optional, default="info")
Logging level: \fBdebug\fR, \fBinfo\fR, \fBwarn\fR, or \fBerror\fR.
.TP
.B audit_enabled (boolean, optional)
Enable audit logging for Docker operations. When absent, the effective value
depends on deployment mode: in system mode (effective UID 0) audit is always
\fBtrue\fR; in user mode it is \fBtrue\fR only when effective \fBlog_level\fR is
\fBdebug\fR, \fBfalse\fR otherwise. An explicit value always overrides the default.
.TP
.B shutdown_timeout (string, optional, default="30s")
Graceful shutdown timeout using Go duration syntax.
.TP
.B operation_retention_ttl (string, optional, default="10m")
Completed operation retention period using Go duration syntax.
.TP
.B operation_max_completed (integer, optional, default=200)
Maximum completed operations to retain in memory. Must be a positive integer.
.TP
.B operation_log_max_bytes (integer, optional, default=4194304)
Maximum operation log size in bytes (default 4 MiB). Must be a positive integer.
.TP
.B trusted_ca_injection (string, optional, default="disabled")
CA injection mode: \fBdisabled\fR (no injection) or \fBauto\fR (automatic injection
using \fBtrusted_ca_path\fR).
.TP
.B trusted_ca_path (string, conditional)
Absolute path to a regular file containing exactly one PEM-encoded
X.509 CA certificate. No additional PEM blocks or content. Required when
\fBtrusted_ca_injection\fR is set to "auto".
.TP
.B http_address (string, optional, default="127.0.0.1:52375")
Loopback TCP listen address for system mode. The host must be exactly
\fB127.0.0.1\fR; the port must be in the range 1..65535.
Changes to \fBhttp_address\fR require daemon restart.
.SH RELOAD BEHAVIOR
Most configuration changes can be applied via \fBdocker-helper reload\fR without
restart. Exceptions:
.IP \(bu 4
\fBhttp_address\fR: Requires daemon restart
.IP \(bu 4
\fBallowed_root\fR: Does NOT automatically update AppArmor; use \fBdocker-helper apparmor root\fR
.SH DERIVED PATHS
.SS System Mode
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/config.json
Configuration file
.TP
.B /etc/docker-helper/admin.token
Admin token
.TP
.B /var/lib/docker-helper/docker-helper.db
SQLite database
.TP
.B /run/docker-helper/docker-helper.sock
Unix socket
.TP
.B /run/docker-helper/mounts/*
Mount-pin runtime directory
.SS User Mode
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/docker-helper/config.json
Configuration file
.TP
.B $XDG_STATE_HOME/docker-helper
State directory (database)
.TP
.B $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/docker-helper
Runtime directory (socket)
.PP
The admin token is always located at \fIdirname(config_path)/admin.token\fR.
When \fBDOCKER_HELPER_CONFIG\fR overrides the config path, the admin token
is also resolved relative to the overridden config directory.
.PP
Principal allowed_roots are stored in the state database, not in \fIconfig.json\fR.
.SH APPARMOR
System mode uses AppArmor confinement with profile \fBdocker-helper-system\fR.
Managed workspace roots are stored in \fI/etc/apparmor.d/docker-helper.d/managed-roots\fR
and can be modified via \fBdocker-helper apparmor root\fR.
.PP
The initial \fBallowed_root\fR from \fBdocker-helper init\fR is added to managed
AppArmor roots. Subsequent changes to configuration or principal allowed roots
do NOT automatically update AppArmor—use \fBdocker-helper apparmor root add PATH\fR
to add new roots.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Minimal configuration (both required fields)
.nf
{
  "allowed_root": "/srv/workspaces",
  "session_ttl": "12h"
}
.fi
.SS Full configuration with all fields
.nf
{
  "allowed_root": "/srv/workspaces",
  "session_ttl": "1h",
  "log_level": "debug",
  "audit_enabled": true,
  "shutdown_timeout": "60s",
  "operation_retention_ttl": "72h",
  "operation_max_completed": 5000,
  "operation_log_max_bytes": 52428800,
  "trusted_ca_injection": "auto",
  "trusted_ca_path": "/etc/docker-helper/ca-bundle.crt",
  "http_address": "127.0.0.1:52376"
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR docker-helper (1),
.BR apparmor (7)
